ranean island of Lampedusa (Italy)</article-title><source>J Quartern Sci</source><year>2004</year><volume>19</volume><fpage>537</fpage><lpage>547</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1002/jqs.853</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B10"><mixed-citation publication-type="book"><article-title>[Bathymetric Map 1]</article-title><source>Menorca to Malta including Thyrrenian Sea. Scale 1:1,000,000</source><year>1986</year><edition>1</edition><publisher-name>Defense Mapping Agency, Washington DC</publisher-name></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B11"><mixed-citation publication-type="book"><article-title>[Bathymetric Map 2]</article-title><source>Mediterranean Sea Rass el Melah Sfax. Scale 1:300,000 (from Italian and French charts to 1991)</source><year>1991</year><publisher-name>Defense Mapping Agency, Washington DC</publisher-name></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B12"><mixed-citation publication-type="book"><name><surname>Flemming</surname><given-names>NC</given-names></name><name><surname>Bailey</surname><given-names>GN</given-names></name><name><surname>Courtillot</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>King</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Lambeck</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Ryerson</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Vita-Finzi</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><article-title>Coastal and marine palaeoenvironments and human dispersal points across the Africa-Eurasia boundary</article-title><source>Maritime Heritage</source><year>2003</year><publisher-name>Malta, Wessex Institute of Technology, University of Malta</publisher-name><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://library.witpress.com/pages/PaperInfo.asp?PaperID=1358">http://library.witpress.com/pages/PaperInfo.asp?PaperID=1358</ext-link></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B13"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Harris</surname><given-names>DJ</given-names></name><name><surname>C